            <ArticleTitle>Chemical abuse and pain management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>247-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article provides additional direction for nurses in altering the pain management plan for individuals who are currently abusing chemicals. There is a definition of terms (i.e., chemical dependence, addiction, physical dependence, tolerance, and cross tolerance), to provide a foundation for this clinical practice. A review of the literature explains theories that explain what we find occurs clinically: that patients who are chemically dependent require more narcotic to control their postoperative pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
